The `state-rw` import is removed, along with the `last-input` write. The linker allows only the interfaces in the node's `with` clause, which are `Clock`, `HTTPClient<['feeds.example.com']>` and `Notifier<'digest'>`. The approval alone doesn't make the component linkable. Once the graph definition grants `StateHandle<…, read-write>`, the import and the `state_rw::put("last-input", &feed_url)` call can go back in unchanged. The node's output is the same either way.

